{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442560130,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM2NTk2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141365967"},"message":"Example:\n\n```\n% datalad -C /tmp create-collection mytest \n2015-09-18 09:08:24,211 [ERROR  ] Protocol: NullProtocol: stderr| warning: no common commits\n| From /tmp/mytest\n|  * [new branch]      master     -\u003e mytest/master (cmd.py:319)\n\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442560213,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM2NjEyMg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141366122"},"message":"And this one seems to be a complicatd way of saying: \"I already have a collection with that name\"\n\n```\n% datalad -C /tmp create-collection mytest \n2015-09-18 09:08:58,264 [ERROR  ] Protocol: NullProtocol: stderr| fatal: remote mytest already exists. (cmd.py:319)\n2015-09-18 09:08:58,264 [ERROR  ] Failed to run ['git', 'remote', 'add', 'mytest', '/tmp/mytest'] under '/home/mih/.local/share/datalad/localcollection'. Exit code=128. out= err=fatal: remote mytest already exists.\n|  (cmd.py:264)\n2015-09-18 09:08:58,265 [ERROR  ] CommandError: command '['git', 'remote', 'add', 'mytest', '/tmp/mytest']' failed with exitcode 128.\n| Failed to run ['git', 'remote', 'add', 'mytest', '/tmp/mytest'] under '/home/mih/.local/share/datalad/localcollection'. Exit code=128. out= err=fatal: remote mytest already exists.\n|  (CommandError) (main.py:206)\n```","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442562847,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM3MzgwNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141373804"},"message":"Yeah, we need to decide, what to do with logging messages in general. If I correctly remember, we've had some preparation of \"log to file instead of tty\" already.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442562970,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM3NDExMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141374111"},"message":"I think those kinds of message should be off by default -- not even in a file. This seems more suitable for --debug. And in that case, they can surely go to the terminal.\n\nMoreover, it would be nice to be consistent and have them all go to stderr -- not sure if that is the case yet.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442563293,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM3NDkwNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141374905"},"message":"Well, there should be some debug-to-file. So, users can send us a proper logfile without being bombarded on terminal.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442563549,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM3NTg1OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141375858"},"message":"Sure, but will should still assume proper functioning by default. User can enable this when needed. I don't want to have an ever increasing logfile that just tracks everything. But again, there is a common way to do this and, in my oppinion, whatever we do we should also support it: all to stderr. Then it is easy for anybody to redirect or silence message with shell tools.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1442564064,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTM3Nzc5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141377791"},"message":"Yes, agree.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442845004,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MTk5NTg3NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-141995874"},"message":"at some point we need to formalize a \"UI\" interface and provide basic implementation (cmdline) while keeping in mind later advanced ones (curses, web ui), so those messages/requests get channeled to the corresponding backend.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1447805873,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE1NzU1MjY4OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/222#issuecomment-157552689"},"message":"At least (since #182) we are not scary by default now (although in my branch any logging would also go to stderr now):\n\n```\n\u003e datalad -C /tmp create-collection mytest \n\u003e\n```\n\nI will close this one for now","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1447805873,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NDY3Mzg2MjAx"},"status":2}]}